<title>JAPAN: ACOM SHARES SLIDE ON STOCK SALES PLAN.</title>
<headline>ACOM SHARES SLIDE ON STOCK SALES PLAN.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Acom Co Ltd slid sharply on Tuesday morning, depressed by news on Monday that it plans to sell up to five million of its shares through a secondary offering, traders said.</p>
<p>Acom, a major consumer finance company, was down 280 yen at 5,920 yen at 0128 GMT, making it the fourth-sharpest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. Its trading volume was 8,000 shares.</p>
